---
/**
 * P1.5 - Why the same amount feels different (metabolism, biology, timing).
 * P2.5 - Gut contents and biological variables.
 * P3.4 - Dietary fats and systemic absorption.
 * Asymmetric bento: 5 items, 5 cells, image + tinted cells for variation.
 */
import { EDIBLES_IMAGE } from '@/data/landing';
---

<section id="variables" class="w-full bg-surface-container-low border-b border-outline-variant/30">
  <div class="max-w-container-max mx-auto px-margin-mobile md:px-margin-desktop py-20 md:py-28">
    <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-stack-md reveal">
      <h2 class="font-headline-lg text-headline-lg text-primary">Why the same amount can feel different</h2>
      <p class="font-body-lg text-body-lg text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
        Two people, the same milligram, the same evening, different arrival. The variables below do the differentiating.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-gutter mt-12 reveal-group">
      <div class="md:col-span-2 bg-surface rounded-xl p-6 sm:p-8 border border-outline-variant/40">
        <h3 class="font-headline-sm text-headline-sm text-primary">Your metabolism</h3>
        <p class="font-body-md text-body-md text-on-surface-variant mt-2 leading-relaxed max-w-[52ch]">
          Liver enzymes set the pace. Fast converters clear an amount quickly and quietly; slow converters feel the same amount linger into the morning. This is why a friend's perfect dose can be your heavy one, and why your own log outranks any generic chart.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="relative rounded-xl overflow-hidden bg-surface-container min-h-48">
        <img
          src={EDIBLES_IMAGE}
          alt="A quiet evening table with herbal tea and a light snack"
          referrerpolicy="no-referrer"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
          class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full object-cover"
          width="640"
          height="480"
        />
      </div>

      <div class="bg-surface rounded-xl p-6 sm:p-8 border border-outline-variant/40">
        <h3 class="font-headline-sm text-headline-sm text-primary">Fat is a multiplier</h3>
        <p class="font-body-sm text-body-sm text-on-surface-variant mt-2 leading-relaxed">
          These compounds are oil-soluble. A fatty snack alongside a swallowed dose can deepen the arrival and stretch it longer.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-surface rounded-xl p-6 sm:p-8 border border-outline-variant/40">
        <h3 class="font-headline-sm text-headline-sm text-primary">What the stomach holds</h3>
        <p class="font-body-sm text-body-sm text-on-surface-variant mt-2 leading-relaxed">
          A full stomach slows every route down. An empty one speeds the sublingual path but can sharpen the edge of the arrival.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-secondary-container/60 rounded-xl p-6 sm:p-8 border border-outline-variant/40">
        <h3 class="font-headline-sm text-headline-sm text-primary">The takeaway</h3>
        <p class="font-body-sm text-body-sm text-on-secondary-container mt-2 leading-relaxed">
          Consistency beats optimisation. Fix the variables you control, then read the results honestly.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
